{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.ConfinementLocalConstancy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.ConfinementLocalConstancy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementLocalConstancy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementLocalConstancy","kind":"theorem","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/confinement-local-constancy.lean#L17-L45","doc":"**Local constancy of confinement level off the phase boundary.**\n\nLet `R` carry a topology (the substrate parameter space `Q`), let\n`B : Set R` be the phase-boundary variety `ℬ`, and let\n`ℓ : R → ℤ` be the confinement level `ℓ(K, ·)` for a fixed knot.\nAway from `ℬ` the level is locally constant: every `q ∉ B` has an\nopen neighborhood `U` on which `ℓ` is constant.\n\n**Hypothesis `hℓ`** is the manuscript's substantive input: off the\nphase boundary `ℬ`, the level is locally constant — every `x ∉ B`\nhas `ℓ` eventually equal to `ℓ x` in its neighborhood filter.  This\nis the property \"the level changes only at `ℬ`\", justified in the\nmanuscript by continuity of the shadow prices `u_λ(q)` (the level is\ndetermined by their sign pattern, locally constant off `ℬ`); that\njustification needs the confinement-level definition over the\nbase-ring topology and is not yet formalised.  Given `hℓ`, the\ntheorem produces the explicit open neighborhood at any `q ∉ B`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:confinement-local-constancy","label":"prop:confinement-local-constancy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/confinement-local-constancy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}